{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775333275-EWI69xEQQiJTu2X0i3Gh","role":"assistant","created":1775333292,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the unemployment insurance taxes data for all states. I need to extract the data for the 50 US states, excluding DC and territories. Let me compile this data:\n\nFrom page 29 and 30:\n- Alabama: 64,332\n- Alaska: 10,983\n- Arizona: 109,606\n- Arkansas: 122,270\n- California: 735,828\n- Colorado: 97,255\n- Connecticut: 64,286\n- Delaware: 27,166\n- District of Columbia: 15,534 (EXCLUDE)\n- Florida: 417,974\n- Georgia: 222,639\n- Hawaii: 17,231\n- Idaho: 34,037\n- Illinois: 271,859\n- Indiana: 100,945\n- Iowa: 49,175\n- Kansas: 66,239\n- Kentucky: 61,165\n- Louisiana: 62,871\n- Maine: 18,204\n- Maryland: 101,598\n- Massachusetts: 161,146\n- Michigan: 178,509\n- Minnesota: 170,442\n- Mississippi: 31,420\n- Missouri: 119,199\n- Montana: 15,993\n- Nebraska: 35,205\n- Nevada: 45,885\n- New Hampshire: 20,345\n- New Jersey: 187,735\n- New Mexico: 19,766\n- New York: 350,082\n- North Carolina: 190,438\n- North Dakota: 12,812\n- Ohio: 235,458\n- Oklahoma: 60,206\n- Oregon: 71,863\n- Pennsylvania: 257,446\n- Rhode Island: 25,975\n- South Carolina: 65,892\n- South Dakota: 12,334\n- Tennessee: 169,376\n- Texas: 536,530\n- Utah: 60,537\n- Vermont: 8,471\n- Virginia: 162,666\n- Washington: 209,293\n- West Virginia: 13,475\n- Wisconsin: 117,667\n\n\n- Wyoming: 7,638\n\nI'll proceed with calculating the Zipf exponent, which involves ranking the state tax data and performing a logarithmic analysis to determine the distribution pattern.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c257914a507c4a9cac3d3fea","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# Unemployment insurance taxes for 50 US states (in thousands of dollars), excluding DC and territories\ndata = {\n    'Alabama': 64332,\n    'Alaska': 10983,\n    'Arizona': 109606,\n    'Arkansas': 122270,\n    'California': 735828,\n    'Colorado': 97255,\n    'Connecticut': 64286,\n    'Delaware': 27166,\n    'Florida': 417974,\n    'Georgia': 222639,\n    'Hawaii': 17231,\n    'Idaho': 34037,\n    'Illinois': 271859,\n    'Indiana': 100945,\n    'Iowa': 49175,\n    'Kansas': 66239,\n    'Kentucky': 61165,\n    'Louisiana': 62871,\n    'Maine': 18204,\n    'Maryland': 101598,\n    'Massachusetts': 161146,\n    'Michigan': 178509,\n    'Minnesota': 170442,\n    'Mississippi': 31420,\n    'Missouri': 119199,\n    'Montana': 15993,\n    'Nebraska': 35205,\n    'Nevada': 45885,\n    'New Hampshire': 20345,\n    'New Jersey': 187735,\n    'New Mexico': 19766,\n    'New York': 350082,\n    'North Carolina': 190438,\n    'North Dakota': 12812,\n    'Ohio': 235458,\n    'Oklahoma': 60206,\n    'Oregon': 71863,\n    'Pennsylvania': 257446,\n    'Rhode Island': 25975,\n    'South Carolina': 65892,\n    'South Dakota': 12334,\n    'Tennessee': 169376,\n    'Texas': 536530,\n    'Utah': 60537,\n    'Vermont': 8471,\n    'Virginia': 162666,\n    'Washington': 209293,\n    'West Virginia': 13475,\n    'Wisconsin': 117667,\n    'Wyoming': 7638\n}\n\n# Sort values in descending order and assign rank (1 = largest)\nsorted_values = sorted(data.values(), reverse=True)\nranks = {v: r+1 for r, v in enumerate(sorted_values)}\n\n# Prepare data for Zipf regression: log(rank) vs log(value)\nlog_ranks = []\nlog_values = []\n\nfor state, value in data.items():\n    rank = ranks[value]\n    log_ranks.append(math.log(rank))\n    log_values.append(math.log(value))\n\n# Linear regression: log(value) = a - s * log(rank)\n# Using least squares\nn = len(log_ranks)\nsum_x = sum(log_ranks)\nsum_y = sum(log_values)\nsum_xy = sum(log_ranks[i] * log_values[i] for i in range(n))\nsum_x2 = sum(x**2 for x in log_ranks)\n\n# Slope (s) and intercept\nslope = (n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y) / (n * sum_x2 - sum_x**2)\nintercept = (sum_y - slope * sum_x) / n\n\n# The Zipf exponent is the absolute value of the slope\nzipf_exponent = -slope\n\nprint(f\"Number of states: {len(data)}\")\nprint(f\"Slope: {slope:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Intercept: {intercept:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Zipf exponent: {zipf_exponent:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Zipf exponent (rounded to thousandth): {round(zipf_exponent, 3)}\")\n\n# Verify by checking the sorted values\nprint(\"\\nTop 5 states by UI tax receipts:\")\nfor i, (state, value) in enumerate(sorted(data.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])[:5]):\n    print(f\"  {i+1}. {state}: {value}\")\n    \nprint(\"\\nBottom 5 states by UI tax receipts:\")\nfor i, (state, value) in enumerate(sorted(data.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])[-5:]):\n    print(f\"  {50-i}. {state}: {value}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
